flashcards.nvim - flashcards in your editor
===========================================

Installation
============
With packer:

    use {
        'git://git.laack.co/flashcards.nvim', 
        commit = "5979f57fc0650df0a280c5cbe1cdea968080bd64"
    }

Keybindings
===========
Put the following in your config file:

    -- default: N/A
    vim.api.nvim_set_keymap('n', '<leader>f', '<Cmd>Flash<CR>', {})
    -- default: right arrow, l
    -- vim.api.nvim_set_keymap('n', '<leader>fn', '<Cmd>NextCard<CR>', {})
    -- default: left arrow, h
    -- vim.api.nvim_set_keymap('n', '<leader>fp', '<Cmd>PreviousCard<CR>', {})
    -- default: up / down arrow, j / k
    -- vim.api.nvim_set_keymap('n', '<leader>ff', '<Cmd>Flip<CR>', {})


Usage
=====
:Flash command expects the cwd to have some files with the .md file extension. In such a directory, this command will open a random flashcard.

The first line of the file must be an H1 header where the associated text is the flashcard's title. The back of the flashcard will be all other lines of the file.
